        {
          "id": "e0341a71-68db-34bf-a422-e109581bc9ee",
          "content": {
            "id": "e0341a71-68db-34bf-a422-e109581bc9ee",
            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "EV maker VinFast's quarterly loss widens on hefty spending",
            "description": "<title><body><p>STORY: VinFast reported a bigger net loss in the third quarter on Friday (November 21).</p><p>It comes after the electric vehicle maker spent heavily to boost sales and expand.</p><p>The loss widened to $910.85 million - significantly up from a year ago.</p><p>The automaker signed two loan facilities during the period totaling $250 million.</p><p>The Vietnamese company wants to grow internationally despite tariff pressures and low-key demand in the U.S.</p><p>But some analysts believe taking on more debt could hit the loss-making firm's margins while it also works hard to cut costs.</p><p>One market watcher said VinFast has shifted its focus from the U.S. and Europe to other Asian markets.</p><p>But added it faces similar challenges competing with Tesla and Chinese EVs.</p><p>However, revenues for the quarter were around $687 million - that's up almost 47% from last year.</p><p>E-scooter and e-bike deliveries soared more than six-fold during the period.</p><p>Shares of the company were down more than 5% in premarket trading.</p></body></title>",
            "summary": "<body><p>STORY: VinFast reported a bigger net loss in the third quarter on Friday (November 21).</p><p>It comes after the electric vehicle maker spent heavily to boost sales and expand.</p><p>The loss widened to $910.85 million - significantly up from a year ago.</p><p>The automaker signed two loan facilities during the period totaling $250 million.</p><p>The Vietnamese company wants to grow internationally despite tariff pressures and low-key demand in the U.S.</p><p>But some analysts believe taking on more debt could hit the loss-making firm's margins while it also works hard to cut costs.</p><p>One market watcher said VinFast has shifted its focus from the U.S. and Europe to other Asian markets.</p><p>But added it faces similar challenges competing with Tesla and Chinese EVs.</p><p>However, revenues for the quarter were around $687 million - that's up almost 47% from last year.</p><p>E-scooter and e-bike deliveries soared more than six-fold during the period.</p><p>Shares of the company were down more than 5% in premarket trading.</p></body>",
